{
  "chapter": "A6",
  "title": "Housekeeping",
  "manualShots": "a6",
  "videos": [
    {
      "id": "A6-01",
      "slug": "A6-01-the-housekeeping-screens",
      "section": "A6.1",
      "title": "The housekeeping screens",
      "intro": {
        "text": "This series is for housekeepers, their supervisors and the desk. In this video you will see the housekeeping screens, and who uses which.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/01.wav",
        "dur": 8.151
      },
      "record": null,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": null,
          "line": {
            "text": "A housekeeper signs in and lands on the Housekeeping board. Their menu is short. Every other screen they may use is one search away.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/02.wav",
            "dur": 7.762
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Housekeeping is the board: every room, what it needs, and who is cleaning it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/03.wav",
            "dur": 4.673
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "Work orders is the list of what needs fixing, and who is fixing it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/04.wav",
            "dur": 4.151
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": 4,
          "line": {
            "text": "Guest requests holds what guests in house have asked for, such as towels, or a broken tap.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/05.wav",
            "dur": 6.218
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": 5,
          "line": {
            "text": "Lost property is what was found, kept until it goes back to its owner.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/06.wav",
            "dur": 4.151
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Rooms shows the house today, as the desk sees it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/07.wav",
            "dur": 3.187
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": 6,
          "line": {
            "text": "The Store and the hotel's equipment have a chapter of their own.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/08.wav",
            "dur": 3.512
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-27",
          "focus": null,
          "line": {
            "text": "The desk also has Wake-up calls: calls to make to guests, on the hotel's clock.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/09.wav",
            "dur": 5.254
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-01",
          "focus": 7,
          "line": {
            "text": "The first time, a Start here card lists the housekeeper's three jobs. Each one opens the screen it happens on. Tap Got it to put it away.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/10.wav",
            "dur": 8.854
          }
        }
      ],
      "checklist": [],
      "outro": {
        "text": "The next videos take each screen, step by step.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-01/11.wav",
        "dur": 3.478
      },
      "next": "The board, and whose rooms are whose"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6-02",
      "slug": "A6-02-the-board-and-whose-rooms-are-whose",
      "section": "A6.2",
      "title": "The board, and whose rooms are whose",
      "intro": {
        "text": "In this video you will read the Housekeeping board, and give rooms to a housekeeper.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/01.wav",
        "dur": 4.499
      },
      "record": null,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "shot": "A6-02",
          "focus": null,
          "line": {
            "text": "Under its title, the board says what it is for: tap a room to move it on. Clean, then inspected.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/02.wav",
            "dur": 6.653
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-02",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Empty rooms shows how many rooms with no guest are clean, out of all of them, and how many are inspected.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/03.wav",
            "dur": 6.38
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-02",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Beside it are six counts: needs cleaning, clean, inspected, in house, due out, and out of service. Tap a count to jump to its rooms.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/04.wav",
            "dur": 8.801
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-02",
          "focus": 4,
          "line": {
            "text": "Each room is a card: its number, type and floor, who is cleaning it, and three buttons. Clean, Inspected, and Repair.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/05.wav",
            "dur": 8.743
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-02",
          "focus": 5,
          "line": {
            "text": "Online means the board is connected. It refreshes by itself, so nobody needs to reload it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/06.wav",
            "dur": 6.026
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-06",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "To give a room to somebody, choose their name on the room's card. It is saved at once.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/07.wav",
            "dur": 5.318
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-06",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "The names along the top count the rooms on each person's sheet.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/08.wav",
            "dur": 3.454
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-07",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "On a phone, a housekeeper taps their own name, and sees only their rooms.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/09.wav",
            "dur": 4.464
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-02",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "All rooms shows every room again. Rooms are given for the business day, so each new day starts unassigned.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/10.wav",
            "dur": 6.642
          }
        }
      ],
      "checklist": [],
      "outro": {
        "text": "A room with a guest leaving today is yellow, and says Due out.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-02/11.wav",
        "dur": 3.779
      },
      "next": "Clean, then inspected"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6-03",
      "slug": "A6-03-clean-then-inspected",
      "section": "A6.4",
      "title": "Clean, then inspected",
      "intro": {
        "text": "In this video you will mark a room clean, then inspected, with a signal and without one.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/01.wav",
        "dur": 5.788
      },
      "record": null,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "shot": "A6-07",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "When the room is clean, tap Clean on its card.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/02.wav",
            "dur": 3.152
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-04",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "A message says so at once, and the room moves to the Clean group.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/03.wav",
            "dur": 3.779
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-04",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Now Inspected is ready. When the room has been checked, tap it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/04.wav",
            "dur": 4.227
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-05",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "The message says the room is inspected.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/05.wav",
            "dur": 2.375
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-05",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "And the room moves under Inspected, ready for the next guest.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/06.wav",
            "dur": 3.605
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-03",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "A grey button cannot be used yet. Tap it anyway, and the card says why.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/07.wav",
            "dur": 5.179
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-03",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Here, the room needs cleaning first. A room is always cleaned before it is inspected.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/08.wav",
            "dur": 5.272
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-08",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "On a stairwell with no signal, the board says Offline. Carry on.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/09.wav",
            "dur": 4.354
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-08",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "Tap Clean as usual. The message says it is saved on this phone, and will be sent when the connection is back.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/10.wav",
            "dur": 6.526
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-08",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Under the title, the board counts the changes waiting to sync.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/11.wav",
            "dur": 3.582
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-09",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "And the room's card says what is queued. When the signal returns, it is sent by itself.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/12.wav",
            "dur": 5.69
          }
        }
      ],
      "checklist": [],
      "outro": {
        "text": "There is no button to send a room for cleaning. A check-out does that by itself.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-03/13.wav",
        "dur": 5.039
      },
      "next": "Something broken, and a room out of service"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6-04",
      "slug": "A6-04-something-broken-and-a-room-out-of-service",
      "section": "A6.6",
      "title": "Something broken, and a room out of service",
      "intro": {
        "text": "Something in a room is broken. In this video you will report a repair, and take a room out of service when it cannot be sold.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/01.wav",
        "dur": 7.431
      },
      "record": null,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "shot": "A6-10",
          "focus": null,
          "line": {
            "text": "On the room's card, tap Repair. Report a repair opens, for that room.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/02.wav",
            "dur": 4.958
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-10",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Type what needs fixing, in a few words.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/03.wav",
            "dur": 2.862
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-10",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "If it is a tagged piece of equipment, choose it here. It then shows as under repair until the repair is closed.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/04.wav",
            "dur": 6.375
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-10",
          "focus": 4,
          "line": {
            "text": "Choose the kind of work, and how urgent it is.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/05.wav",
            "dur": 3.002
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-11",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Most repairs do not take the room out of service. If this one must, tick Take the room out of service too.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/06.wav",
            "dur": 6.804
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-11",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Then say why it is coming out, from which date, and until when. Leave Until empty if nobody knows.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/07.wav",
            "dur": 6.34
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-11",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "Tap Raise it. The repair goes on Work orders.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/08.wav",
            "dur": 3.321
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-11",
          "focus": 4,
          "line": {
            "text": "A room that must come out with no repair, for a refurbishment or for house use, uses Out of service without a repair.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/09.wav",
            "dur": 7.216
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-12",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Choose why it is coming out, set the dates, and write what is actually wrong.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/10.wav",
            "dur": 4.859
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-12",
          "focus": 5,
          "line": {
            "text": "Then tap Take out of service. A room with a guest in it cannot be taken out.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/11.wav",
            "dur": 5.144
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-13",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "The room moves to Out of service, and is not sold.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/12.wav",
            "dur": 3.048
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-13",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "When it is ready again, tap Put back.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/13.wav",
            "dur": 2.642
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-14",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "The window lists each period the room is out, with its dates.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/14.wav",
            "dur": 3.559
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-14",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Tap Put back beside the one that is over. The room comes back needing cleaning, unless the hotel has chosen otherwise.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/15.wav",
            "dur": 7.396
          }
        }
      ],
      "checklist": [],
      "outro": {
        "text": "A repair can wait on the phone with no signal. Taking a room out, and putting it back, need the connection.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-04/16.wav",
        "dur": 6.409
      },
      "next": "Work orders"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6-05",
      "slug": "A6-05-work-orders",
      "section": "A6.8",
      "title": "Work orders",
      "intro": {
        "text": "Work orders is the list of what needs fixing. In this video you will start a repair, record what it cost, and close it.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/01.wav",
        "dur": 7.524
      },
      "record": null,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "shot": "A6-15",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Open lists what is still to fix: the most urgent first, and the oldest first within that.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/02.wav",
            "dur": 5.765
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-15",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "Each one says what needs fixing, and how urgent it is.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/03.wav",
            "dur": 3.884
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-15",
          "focus": 4,
          "line": {
            "text": "Under it: the room, the kind, who raised it and when, how long it has been open, and who has it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/04.wav",
            "dur": 5.498
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-15",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Raise one opens the same form as the room's Repair button.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/05.wav",
            "dur": 3.71
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-16",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Here you type the room. Leave it empty for anything that is not a room, such as a lift or the lobby.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/06.wav",
            "dur": 6.015
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-15",
          "focus": 5,
          "line": {
            "text": "When somebody begins the work, tap Start.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/07.wav",
            "dur": 2.897
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-17",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "The repair now says Being fixed.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/08.wav",
            "dur": 2.119
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-18",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Costs records what the repair cost, in rupees.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/09.wav",
            "dur": 3.536
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-18",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "Every cost needs its proof: a photo or screenshot of the bill, the payment or the transaction. Without it, the cost is not recorded.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/10.wav",
            "dur": 8.383
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-18",
          "focus": 4,
          "line": {
            "text": "Then tap Record the cost. A wrong cost is cancelled with a reason, never deleted.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/11.wav",
            "dur": 5.748
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-19",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "When the work is finished, tap Close, and write what was done. It is the line somebody reads the next time this breaks.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/12.wav",
            "dur": 7.234
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-19",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "Then tap Fixed. Or Not needed, if it needed no fixing after all.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/13.wav",
            "dur": 5.074
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-20",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Closed keeps every closed repair.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/14.wav",
            "dur": 2.375
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-20",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "With what was done. A bill that arrives after the close can still be recorded here, with Costs.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/15.wav",
            "dur": 5.829
          }
        }
      ],
      "checklist": [],
      "outro": {
        "text": "Costs are recorded by the owner, an administrator, the G M, the hotel manager or the Inventory Manager. Everybody else sees the repair without the money.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-05/16.wav",
        "dur": 9.8
      },
      "next": "Guest requests"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6-06",
      "slug": "A6-06-guest-requests",
      "section": "A6.9",
      "title": "Guest requests",
      "intro": {
        "text": "A guest asks for towels, or says the tap is broken. In this video you will raise a request, take it, and mark it done.",
        "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/01.wav",
        "dur": 7.942
      },
      "record": null,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "shot": "A6-21",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Tap New request, and choose the room. Only guests in house now are listed.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/02.wav",
            "dur": 4.981
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-21",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "Choose the team it is for: Housekeeping, Something broken, or Food and drink.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/03.wav",
            "dur": 4.801
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-21",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "Say what is wanted.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/04.wav",
            "dur": 1.504
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-21",
          "focus": 4,
          "line": {
            "text": "And when, only if the guest said.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/05.wav",
            "dur": 2.769
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-21",
          "focus": 5,
          "line": {
            "text": "Then tap Raise it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/06.wav",
            "dur": 1.376
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-22",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "The request waits under Open, with the room, who raised it, how long it has waited, and who has it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/07.wav",
            "dur": 6.067
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-23",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "A housekeeper sees only their own teams: housekeeping, and something broken.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/08.wav",
            "dur": 4.639
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-23",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "They tap Take it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/09.wav",
            "dur": 1.411
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-24",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "It now says Being done.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/10.wav",
            "dur": 1.852
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-24",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "And everyone can see who has it.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/11.wav",
            "dur": 2.154
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-24",
          "focus": 3,
          "line": {
            "text": "When it is done, tap Done. A housekeeping request closes with one tap. Something broken asks what was done, and is also on Work orders.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/12.wav",
            "dur": 9.098
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-25",
          "focus": 1,
          "line": {
            "text": "Done, last 24 hours, lists what was finished.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/13.wav",
            "dur": 3.721
          }
        },
        {
          "shot": "A6-25",
          "focus": 2,
          "line": {
            "text": "With how long each took, and who did it. There are no time targets: nothing turns red.",
            "voice": "a6/voice/A6-06/14.wav",
            "dur": 5.399
